From 6e4a330629e830cdb3379df60aa493f176d0f10e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <dev@phlink.local>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:54:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 10.06 UpdaterServiceFactory + KeyedService

Two small changes to make UpdaterService consumable from the rest of
the browser without having to plumb it through ProfileImpl:

  1. UpdaterService now inherits from KeyedService (single virtual
     ~Shutdown method, no behavior change; ~UpdaterService is now
     'override').

  2. New UpdaterServiceFactory (ProfileKeyedServiceFactory):
       - GetForProfile(Profile*) -> UpdaterService*
       - GetInstance() singleton via base::NoDestructor.
       - EnsureFactoryBuilt() so the future settings WebUI handler
         (10-06b) can opt-in once at startup without us having to
         touch chrome_browser_main_extra_parts_profiles.cc (huge,
         rebase-fragile).
       - ProfileSelections: regular-original-only; guest / system /
         ash-internals all kNone.
       - ServiceIsCreatedWithBrowserContext = false (lazy).
       - BuildServiceInstanceForBrowserContext binds a no-op
         CheckCallback for now; the real wiring of
         UpdateCheckPipeline::Run (which already exists per 10-02e)
         happens in the follow-up that adds the chrome://settings/help
         WebUI integration.
       - Updater prefs live in local state, not profile prefs;
         RegisterProfilePrefs is intentionally empty.

Tests: factory singleton invariant + EnsureFactoryBuilt idempotence.
Profile-keyed selection itself is exercised by Chromium's own
keyed-service test infrastructure; we don't duplicate TestingProfile
plumbing here.

32/32 phlink_updater_unittests pass; chrome builds + codesigns.
Refs phlink phase 10-06.
